  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-06-12T07:55:52.594Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I tried to look if it was already suggested but I didn't find anything, so I try to do it myself.\n\nIt would be very useful in my opinion for those who create worlds the possibility of having a sort of local multiplayer to be able to test the various functions. A short time ago I posted a bug in which the Local doesn't work well, so in trying to find a solution as soon as possible, so I'm doing various experiments with the Trigger, the problem is, to see if what I'm doing works I have to upload every time the world (and considering that my internet is very slow it takes even more than 2 hours) and then ask someone if he can enter my world just to see if the Trigger acts as it should.\n\nOne thing that I thought was to take advantage of the \"Number of clients\" option, essentially instead of being separate instances they all go in the same instance. Then I guess there is the problem that there can't be the same player for all instances, so I thought of a sort of \"visitor\" account with a default avatar, essentially in the first instance of the game there will be the account of the map creator, while the other instances will have this visitor account. \nForgive me if I have not explained myself very well, I don't speak English very well",
